Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||07-03-2001||11:48 PM||||Well I changes the TPS and the MAP one night and it didn't do much.  SO, with a little of the money I got for the RX-7 I sold I got a new IAC valve.  Put it in and drove around for awhile and it didn't seem to do much, BUT I drove around for maybe 50 or 60 miles today and it is running GREAT!  Also, with the rest of the money I got for the RX-7 I Ordered a new Wrap Around Dash from PISA!!  The guy there said that Dan will be calling me on Thursday to Confirm my order and since they make them per order it will be about 2 weeks before it is finished being made and delivered in about 3 weeks!!  I'll take tons of pics of the removal of the stock dash and the installation of the new wrap Around and post them on my site along with any problems I run into or any tips I figure out.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-04-2001||12:33 AM||||Let me know how good that dash is and how much you like it, I'm looking at that for the future.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg"> <BR>AIM - DecadenceR||||reg||1
Z||000002||3fifty||07-04-2001||01:26 AM||||The wrap around dash is nice, but you do not just swap your trim from the original dash. You must work the corners and trim areas where the ac vents go. There is only one hole<BR>in each speaker cut out to mount to the firewall where the factory has two. There are no holes in the dash where the factory radio bezel has tabs on the sides. As soon as I tie up the wires for my alarm, I am ready to put the dash in. I will try to keep everyone posted.<P>3fifty one day!!!!!!||||reg||1
